# Line-ending policy: every tracked text file is normalized to LF in the
# index and checked out as LF on every platform, so a fresh clone is
# byte-identical to the release manifest whether it lands on Windows, macOS
# or Linux (a different core.autocrlf / editor setting cannot alter a
# checkout). The .sh entry points in particular must keep LF: a CRLF
# checkout breaks the shebang on macOS ("bad interpreter" / stray \r — see
# TEST-PLAN-MAC.md, failure signatures).
* text=auto eol=lf
